      "leaf_matches": [
        {
          "slug": "clinical-data-management",
          "reason": "README identifies LibreClinica as open-source EDC/CDM software. The official investigator and monitor manuals document the governed study record (subjects under sites, events and CRFs), design-time validation with automatic 'Failed Validation Check' discrepancies, four discrepancy types including Query and Reason for Change, assignment/reply/close statuses (New, Updated, Resolution Proposed, Closed), the rule that discrepancy notes cannot be deleted, mandatory reason-for-change when editing completed CRFs, SDV, electronic signatures, CRF-level Completed/Locked statuses, and a study audit log. Study-level database-lock gating, unlock/re-lock and external-data/coding reconciliation are not directly evidenced, so those claims are not made. GitHub metadata confirms repository id 169558966. License: the official project page states LibreClinica is published under LGPL-3.0; the GitHub license API reports LGPL-3.0 and its content is the GPL-3.0 base text that LGPLv3 explicitly incorporates, while COPYING.LESSER carries the LGPL-3.0 additional permissions. This resolves the earlier ambiguity rather than treating the GPL-3.0 base text as a contradiction.",
